-- title:
--   Swapping the two coordinates of a Drinfeld chart presentation
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $O$ a commutative ring and $\varpi \in O$, and let $pr$ be a chart presentation of type `ChartPresentation q O ϖ`, that is: power series $f, u, v \in O[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u$ and $v$ units and with $f - (X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1)$ lying in the $(q+2)$-nd power of the ideal $(X_0, X_1)$ of $O[[X_0,X_1]]$; write $\sigma$ for `MvPowerSeries.rename` along the transposition `Equiv.swap (0 : Fin 2) 1`, the exchange of the two variables. The assertion is that there exist a further chart presentation $pr'$ of the same type and a ring isomorphism $e$ from $pr$'s chart ring to $pr'$'s chart ring — each being the quotient of $O[[X_0,X_1]]$ by the principal ideal generated by the element `rel` attached to the presentation in question — such that $e$ carries the class of the constant series $C\,o$ to the class of $C\,o$ for every $o \in O$, carries the class of $X_0$ to the class of $X_1$ and the class of $X_1$ to the class of $X_0$, and such that the data of $pr'$ are $v' = \sigma(v)$, $u' = -\sigma(u)$ and $f' = -\sigma(f)$.
--
--   This records the symmetry of the local Drinfeld chart in its two coordinates: the Drinfeld form $X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ is antisymmetric under the exchange of variables, so the swapped data become a presentation again only after inserting signs in $f$ and $u$. It is used in the analysis of the blow-up chart of a Drinfeld chart, specifically in [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_blowupChartAt_uvCrossingModel_pow_of_X_one_div_not_mem`](thm.html#DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_blowupChartAt_uvCrossingModel_pow_of_X_one_div_not_mem), where it allows the two coordinates to be interchanged and thus one of two symmetric cases to be reduced to the other.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart_ChartPresentation_exists_swap_ringEquiv.lean

import Mathlib.RingTheory.MvPowerSeries.Rename
import Definitions.Def_DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

open MvPowerSeries IsLocalRing DrinfeldCurve DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart

theorem DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.ChartPresentation.exists_swap_ringEquiv
    (q : ℕ) [Fact q.Prime] (O : Type) [CommRing O] (ϖ : O) (pr : ChartPresentation q O ϖ) :
    ∃ (pr' : ChartPresentation q O ϖ) (e : pr.Ring ≃+* pr'.Ring),
      (∀ o : O, e (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (C o)) = Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (C o)) ∧
      e (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (X 0)) = Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (X 1) ∧
      e (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (X 1)) = Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (X 0) ∧
      pr'.v = MvPowerSeries.rename (Equiv.swap (0 : Fin 2) 1) pr.v ∧
      pr'.u = -MvPowerSeries.rename (Equiv.swap (0 : Fin 2) 1) pr.u ∧
      pr'.f = -MvPowerSeries.rename (Equiv.swap (0 : Fin 2) 1) pr.f := by sorry
